:HELP NAME=CHGSAVF.Change Save File (CHGSAVF)
:P.Use the Change Save File (CHGSAVF) command to change a save file's
attributes.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSAVF/FILE'.Save file (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSAVF/MAXRCDS'.Maximum records (MAXRCDS)
:P.The most records a spooled file may hold. *NOMAX sets no limit.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 2147483647.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSAVF/TEXT'.Text 'description' (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSAVF/WAITFILE'.Maximum file wait time (WAITFILE)
:P.How many seconds the program waits for the file's resources to become
available when the file is opened. *IMMED does not wait; *CLS uses the
job's class.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.The program does not wait.
:PT.:PK.*CLS:EPK.
:PD.The default wait time of the job's class.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGSAVF/SHARE'.Share open data path (SHARE)
:P.Whether the open data path of the file is shared with other programs
of the job that open it with SHARE(*YES)&colon. they then share the
file's position and buffers.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The program gets an open data path of its own.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The open data path is shared.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CLRSAVF.Clear Save File (CLRSAVF)
:P.Use the Clear Save File (CLRSAVF) command to empty a save file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CLRSAVF/FILE'.Save file (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTSAVF.Create Save File (CRTSAVF)
:P.Use the Create Save File (CRTSAVF) command to create a save file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSAVF/FILE'.Save file (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSAVF/TEXT'.Text 'description' (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSAVF/MAXRCDS'.Maximum records (MAXRCDS)
:P.The most records a spooled file may hold. *NOMAX sets no limit.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 2147483647.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSAVF/ASP'.Auxiliary storage pool ID (ASP)
:P.The auxiliary storage pool the object is put in.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 255.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LIBASP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSAVF/WAITFILE'.Maximum file wait time (WAITFILE)
:P.How many seconds the program waits for the file's resources to become
available when the file is opened. *IMMED does not wait; *CLS uses the
job's class.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*IMMED:EPK.
:PD.The program does not wait.
:PT.:PK.*CLS:EPK.
:PD.The default wait time of the job's class.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32767.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSAVF/SHARE'.Share open data path (SHARE)
:P.Whether the open data path of the file is shared with other programs
of the job that open it with SHARE(*YES)&colon. they then share the
file's position and buffers.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The program gets an open data path of its own.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The open data path is shared.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTSAVF/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPSAVF.Display Save File (DSPSAVF)
:P.Use the Display Save File (DSPSAVF) command to show what a save file
holds (save files come later).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSAVF/FILE'.Save file (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPSAVF/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RSTAUT.Restore Authority (RSTAUT)
:P.Use the Restore Authority (RSTAUT) command to grant the private
authorities restored with the profiles.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTAUT/USRPRF'.User profile (USRPRF)
:P.The user profile the command uses.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTAUT/SAVASPDEV'.Saved ASP device (SAVASPDEV)
:P.The saved ASP device for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*SYSBAS:EPK.
:PD.The system ASP and the basic user ASPs.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTAUT/ASPDEV'.Restore to ASP device (ASPDEV)
:P.The auxiliary storage pool device the command works in&colon. the
system ASP and basic user ASPs, or an independent ASP group.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAVASPDEV:EPK.
:PD.The ASP device the object was saved from.
:PT.:PK.*SYSBAS:EPK.
:PD.The system ASP and the basic user ASPs.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RSTCFG.Restore Configuration (RSTCFG)
:P.Use the Restore Configuration (RSTCFG) command to restore
configuration objects.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTCFG/OBJ'.Objects (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTCFG/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SAVF:EPK.
:PD.A save file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MEDDFN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTCFG/OBJTYPE'.Object types (OBJTYPE)
:P.The type or types of the objects the command works on.
:P.Up to 10 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.Device descriptions.
:PT.:PK.*CTLD:EPK.
:PD.Controller descriptions.
:PT.:PK.*LIND:EPK.
:PD.Line descriptions.
:PT.:PK.*CNNL:EPK.
:PD.Connection lists.
:PT.:PK.*COSD:EPK.
:PD.Class-of-service descriptions.
:PT.:PK.*NWID:EPK.
:PD.Network interface descriptions.
:PT.:PK.*NWSD:EPK.
:PD.Network server descriptions.
:PT.:PK.*NTBD:EPK.
:PD.NetBIOS descriptions.
:PT.:PK.*CFGL:EPK.
:PD.Configuration lists.
:PT.:PK.*CSI:EPK.
:PD.Communications side information.
:PT.:PK.*IPXD:EPK.
:PD.IPX descriptions.
:PT.:PK.*MODD:EPK.
:PD.Mode descriptions.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CRGM.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTCFG/VOL'.Volume identifier (VOL)
:P.The volume identifier of the tape or optical volume. *MOUNTED uses
whatever volume is in the device.
:P.Up to 75 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*MOUNTED:EPK.
:PD.Whatever volume is in the device.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTCFG/SEQNBR'.Sequence number (SEQNBR)
:P.The sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SEARCH:EPK.
:PD.The value is searched for.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16777215.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTCFG/LABEL'.File label (LABEL)
:P.The label of the file on the volume.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 17 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SAVCFG.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTCFG/ENDOPT'.End of media option (ENDOPT)
:P.What the device does with the tape when the operation ends&colon.
leave it where it is, rewind it, or rewind and unload it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REWIND:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound.
:PT.:PK.*LEAVE:EPK.
:PD.The tape stays where it is; the next operation goes on from there.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTCFG/SAVF'.Save file (SAVF)
:P.The save file, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTCFG/MEDDFN'.Media definition (MEDDFN)
:P.The media definition, which lists the devices and settings a parallel
save or restore uses.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTCFG/OPTFILE'.Optical file (OPTFILE)
:P.The path of the file on the optical volume.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, '*' is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTCFG/SRM'.System Resource Management (SRM)
:P.The system Resource Management for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTCFG/ALWOBJDIF'.Allow object differences (ALWOBJDIF)
:P.Which differences between the saved object and the object on the
system are allowed when it is restored.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTCFG/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PK.*OUTFILE:EPK.
:PD.The output goes to the database file named by OUTFILE.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTCFG/OUTFILE'.File to receive output (OUTFILE)
:P.The database file that receives the output when OUTPUT(*OUTFILE) is
given. The file is created with the system's model format when it does
not exist.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTCFG/OUTMBR'.Output member options (OUTMBR)
:P.The member of the output file that receives the records, and whether
they replace the member's records or are added after them.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Member to receive output
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first member of the file. A member with the file's name is added
when the file has none.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Replace or add records
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.The member's records are cleared first.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The records are added after the member's records.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTCFG/INFTYPE'.Type of output information (INFTYPE)
:P.The type of output information for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*MBR:EPK.
:PD.The member.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RSTLIB.Restore Library (RSTLIB)
:P.Use the Restore Library (RSTLIB) command to restore saved libraries
from a device or a save file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/SAVLIB'.Saved library (SAVLIB)
:P.The saved library for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NONSYS, *IBM.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SAVF:EPK.
:PD.A save file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MEDDFN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/VOL'.Volume identifier (VOL)
:P.The volume identifier of the tape or optical volume. *MOUNTED uses
whatever volume is in the device.
:P.Up to 75 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*MOUNTED:EPK.
:PD.Whatever volume is in the device.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/SEQNBR'.Sequence number (SEQNBR)
:P.The sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SEARCH:EPK.
:PD.The value is searched for.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16777215.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/LABEL'.File label (LABEL)
:P.The label of the file on the volume.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAVLIB:EPK.
:PD.The library the object was saved from.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 17 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/ENDOPT'.End of media option (ENDOPT)
:P.What the device does with the tape when the operation ends&colon.
leave it where it is, rewind it, or rewind and unload it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REWIND:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound.
:PT.:PK.*LEAVE:EPK.
:PD.The tape stays where it is; the next operation goes on from there.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/STRLIB'.Starting library (STRLIB)
:P.The starting library for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/OPTION'.Option (OPTION)
:P.The option for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*NEW:EPK.
:PD.A new one.
:PT.:PK.*OLD:EPK.
:PD.The old one.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FREE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/MBROPT'.Database member option (MBROPT)
:P.What happens to an existing member that receives data&colon. its
records are replaced, or the new records are added after them.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*NEW:EPK.
:PD.A new one.
:PT.:PK.*OLD:EPK.
:PD.The old one.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MATCH.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/SPLFDTA'.Spooled file data (SPLFDTA)
:P.Whether the data of spooled files is saved with the output queues.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NEW:EPK.
:PD.A new one.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/SAVF'.Save file (SAVF)
:P.The save file, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/MEDDFN'.Media definition (MEDDFN)
:P.The media definition, which lists the devices and settings a parallel
save or restore uses.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/OPTFILE'.Optical file (OPTFILE)
:P.The path of the file on the optical volume.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, '*' is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/ALWOBJDIF'.Allow object differences (ALWOBJDIF)
:P.Which differences between the saved object and the object on the
system are allowed when it is restored.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*OWNER:EPK.
:PD.The owner of the object.
:PT.:PK.*PGP:EPK.
:PD.The primary group.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *COMPATIBLE, *AUTL, *FILELVL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/RSTLIB'.Restore to library (RSTLIB)
:P.The restore to library for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAVLIB:EPK.
:PD.The library the object was saved from.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/SAVASPDEV'.Saved ASP device (SAVASPDEV)
:P.The saved ASP device for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PK.*SYSBAS:EPK.
:PD.The system ASP and the basic user ASPs.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/SAVASP'.Saved ASP number (SAVASP)
:P.The saved ASP number for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/RSTASPDEV'.Restore to ASP device (RSTASPDEV)
:P.The restore to ASP device for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAVASPDEV:EPK.
:PD.The ASP device the object was saved from.
:PT.:PK.*SYSBAS:EPK.
:PD.The system ASP and the basic user ASPs.
:PT.:PK.*CURASPGRP:EPK.
:PD.The ASP group of the job's current thread.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/RSTASP'.Restore to ASP number (RSTASP)
:P.The restore to ASP number for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 32.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SAVASP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PK.*OUTFILE:EPK.
:PD.The output goes to the database file named by OUTFILE.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/OUTFILE'.File to receive output (OUTFILE)
:P.The database file that receives the output when OUTPUT(*OUTFILE) is
given. The file is created with the system's model format when it does
not exist.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/OUTMBR'.Output member options (OUTMBR)
:P.The member of the output file that receives the records, and whether
they replace the member's records or are added after them.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Member to receive output
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first member of the file. A member with the file's name is added
when the file has none.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Replace or add records
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.The member's records are cleared first.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The records are added after the member's records.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/INFTYPE'.Type of output information (INFTYPE)
:P.The type of output information for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*MBR:EPK.
:PD.The member.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/OMITLIB'.Libraries to omit (OMITLIB)
:P.Libraries that are not to be included.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/OMITOBJ'.Objects to omit (OMITOBJ)
:P.Objects that are not to be included.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Object
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Object type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
