:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/FRCOBJCVN'.Force object conversion (FRCOBJCVN)
:P.The force object conversion for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Convert
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Objects to convert
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*RQD:EPK.
:PD.A value is required.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTLIB/DFRID'.Defer ID (DFRID)
:P.The defer ID for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RSTOBJ.Restore Object (RSTOBJ)
:P.Use the Restore Object (RSTOBJ) command to restore objects saved from
a library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/OBJ'.Objects (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/SAVLIB'.Saved library (SAVLIB)
:P.The saved library for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SAVF:EPK.
:PD.A save file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MEDDFN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/OBJTYPE'.Object types (OBJTYPE)
:P.The type or types of the objects the command works on.
:P.Up to 72 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/VOL'.Volume identifier (VOL)
:P.The volume identifier of the tape or optical volume. *MOUNTED uses
whatever volume is in the device.
:P.Up to 75 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*MOUNTED:EPK.
:PD.Whatever volume is in the device.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/SEQNBR'.Sequence number (SEQNBR)
:P.The sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SEARCH:EPK.
:PD.The value is searched for.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16777215.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/LABEL'.File label (LABEL)
:P.The label of the file on the volume.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAVLIB:EPK.
:PD.The library the object was saved from.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 17 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/ENDOPT'.End of media option (ENDOPT)
:P.What the device does with the tape when the operation ends&colon.
leave it where it is, rewind it, or rewind and unload it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REWIND:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound.
:PT.:PK.*LEAVE:EPK.
:PD.The tape stays where it is; the next operation goes on from there.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/SAVF'.Save file (SAVF)
:P.The save file, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/MEDDFN'.Media definition (MEDDFN)
:P.The media definition, which lists the devices and settings a parallel
save or restore uses.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/OPTFILE'.Optical file (OPTFILE)
:P.The path of the file on the optical volume.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, '*' is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/OPTION'.Option (OPTION)
:P.The option for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*NEW:EPK.
:PD.A new one.
:PT.:PK.*OLD:EPK.
:PD.The old one.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FREE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/MBROPT'.Database member option (MBROPT)
:P.What happens to an existing member that receives data&colon. its
records are replaced, or the new records are added after them.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*NEW:EPK.
:PD.A new one.
:PT.:PK.*OLD:EPK.
:PD.The old one.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MATCH.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/SPLFDTA'.Spooled file data (SPLFDTA)
:P.Whether the data of spooled files is saved with the output queues.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NEW:EPK.
:PD.A new one.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/ALWOBJDIF'.Allow object differences (ALWOBJDIF)
:P.Which differences between the saved object and the object on the
system are allowed when it is restored.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*OWNER:EPK.
:PD.The owner of the object.
:PT.:PK.*PGP:EPK.
:PD.The primary group.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *COMPATIBLE, *AUTL, *FILELVL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/RSTLIB'.Restore to library (RSTLIB)
:P.The restore to library for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAVLIB:EPK.
:PD.The library the object was saved from.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/SAVASPDEV'.Saved ASP device (SAVASPDEV)
:P.The saved ASP device for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ANY:EPK.
:PD.Any value matches.
:PT.:PK.*SYSBAS:EPK.
:PD.The system ASP and the basic user ASPs.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/RSTASPDEV'.Restore to ASP device (RSTASPDEV)
:P.The restore to ASP device for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAVASPDEV:EPK.
:PD.The ASP device the object was saved from.
:PT.:PK.*SYSBAS:EPK.
:PD.The system ASP and the basic user ASPs.
:PT.:PK.*CURASPGRP:EPK.
:PD.The ASP group of the job's current thread.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/FILEMBR'.File member (FILEMBR)
:P.The file member for this command.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. File
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Member
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/PVTAUT'.Private authorities (PVTAUT)
:P.Whether to private authorities.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PK.*OUTFILE:EPK.
:PD.The output goes to the database file named by OUTFILE.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/OUTFILE'.File to receive output (OUTFILE)
:P.The database file that receives the output when OUTPUT(*OUTFILE) is
given. The file is created with the system's model format when it does
not exist.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/OUTMBR'.Output member options (OUTMBR)
:P.The member of the output file that receives the records, and whether
they replace the member's records or are added after them.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Member to receive output
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first member of the file. A member with the file's name is added
when the file has none.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Replace or add records
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.The member's records are cleared first.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The records are added after the member's records.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/INFTYPE'.Type of output information (INFTYPE)
:P.The type of output information for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*MBR:EPK.
:PD.The member.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/OMITOBJ'.Objects to omit (OMITOBJ)
:P.Objects that are not to be included.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Object
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Object type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ALRTBL:EPK.
:PD.Alert tables.
