:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/FRCOBJCVN'.Force object conversion (FRCOBJCVN)
:P.The force object conversion for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Convert
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Objects to convert
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*RQD:EPK.
:PD.A value is required.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTOBJ/DFRID'.Defer ID (DFRID)
:P.The defer ID for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RSTUSRPRF.Restore User Profiles (RSTUSRPRF)
:P.Use the Restore User Profiles (RSTUSRPRF) command to restore user
profiles and authorization lists.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTUSRPRF/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SAVF:EPK.
:PD.A save file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MEDDFN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTUSRPRF/USRPRF'.User profile (USRPRF)
:P.The user profile the command uses.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*NEW:EPK.
:PD.A new one.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTUSRPRF/OMITUSRPRF'.User profiles to omit (OMITUSRPRF)
:P.The user profiles to omit for this command.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTUSRPRF/SECDTA'.Security data (SECDTA)
:P.The security data for this command.
:P.Up to 3 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*USRPRF:EPK.
:PD.The value of the user profile the job runs under.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PWDGRP, *PVTAUT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTUSRPRF/VOL'.Volume identifier (VOL)
:P.The volume identifier of the tape or optical volume. *MOUNTED uses
whatever volume is in the device.
:P.Up to 75 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*MOUNTED:EPK.
:PD.Whatever volume is in the device.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTUSRPRF/SEQNBR'.Sequence number (SEQNBR)
:P.The sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SEARCH:EPK.
:PD.The value is searched for.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16777215.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTUSRPRF/ENDOPT'.End of media option (ENDOPT)
:P.What the device does with the tape when the operation ends&colon.
leave it where it is, rewind it, or rewind and unload it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REWIND:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound.
:PT.:PK.*LEAVE:EPK.
:PD.The tape stays where it is; the next operation goes on from there.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTUSRPRF/SAVF'.Save file (SAVF)
:P.The save file, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTUSRPRF/MEDDFN'.Media definition (MEDDFN)
:P.The media definition, which lists the devices and settings a parallel
save or restore uses.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTUSRPRF/OPTFILE'.Optical file (OPTFILE)
:P.The path of the file on the optical volume.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, '*' is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTUSRPRF/ALWOBJDIF'.Allow object differences (ALWOBJDIF)
:P.Which differences between the saved object and the object on the
system are allowed when it is restored.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTUSRPRF/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PK.*OUTFILE:EPK.
:PD.The output goes to the database file named by OUTFILE.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTUSRPRF/OUTFILE'.File to receive output (OUTFILE)
:P.The database file that receives the output when OUTPUT(*OUTFILE) is
given. The file is created with the system's model format when it does
not exist.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTUSRPRF/OUTMBR'.Output member options (OUTMBR)
:P.The member of the output file that receives the records, and whether
they replace the member's records or are added after them.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Member to receive output
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first member of the file. A member with the file's name is added
when the file has none.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Replace or add records
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.The member's records are cleared first.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The records are added after the member's records.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RSTUSRPRF/INFTYPE'.Type of output information (INFTYPE)
:P.The type of output information for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*MBR:EPK.
:PD.The member.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SAV.Save Object (SAV)
:P.Use the Save Object (SAV) command to save IFS objects.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAV/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAV/OBJ'.Objects (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Name
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, '*' is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Include or omit
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.Included.
:PT.:PK.*OMIT:EPK.
:PD.Left out.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAV/PATTERN'.Name pattern (PATTERN)
:P.The name pattern for this command.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Pattern
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Include or omit
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.Included.
:PT.:PK.*OMIT:EPK.
:PD.Left out.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAV/SUBTREE'.Directory subtree (SUBTREE)
:P.Whether the objects in the subdirectories are included.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.The directory and everything below it.
:PT.:PK.*DIR:EPK.
:PD.The directory and the objects in it, but not its subdirectories'
contents.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.The objects of the directory only.
:PT.:PK.*OBJ:EPK.
:PD.The object only.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *STG.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAV/SAVACT'.Save active (SAVACT)
:P.Whether objects in use can be saved, and at which point of
consistency.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SYNC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAV/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAV/VOL'.Volume identifier (VOL)
:P.The volume identifier of the tape or optical volume. *MOUNTED uses
whatever volume is in the device.
:P.Up to 75 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*MOUNTED:EPK.
:PD.Whatever volume is in the device.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAV/LABEL'.Label (LABEL)
:P.The label of the file on the volume.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*GEN:EPK.
:PD.Generated by the system.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 17 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAV/OPTFILE'.Optical file (OPTFILE)
:P.The path of the file on the optical volume.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, '*' is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAV/SEQNBR'.Sequence number (SEQNBR)
:P.The sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16777215.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAV/ENDOPT'.End of media option (ENDOPT)
:P.What the device does with the tape when the operation ends&colon.
leave it where it is, rewind it, or rewind and unload it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REWIND:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound.
:PT.:PK.*LEAVE:EPK.
:PD.The tape stays where it is; the next operation goes on from there.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAV/SYSTEM'.Save from system (SYSTEM)
:P.The save from system for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LCL:EPK.
:PD.Local.
:PT.:PK.*RMT:EPK.
:PD.Remote.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAV/PRECHK'.Object pre-check (PRECHK)
:P.Whether every object is checked before any is saved or restored, and
the operation stopped if any cannot be.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAV/TGTRLS'.Target release (TGTRLS)
:P.The release of the operating system the object is created for.
*CURRENT is this release; *PRV is the previous one.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.This release.
:PT.:PK.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAV/UPDHST'.Update history (UPDHST)
:P.Whether the save history of the objects is updated.
:P.Up to 2 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*SYS:EPK.
:PD.The system's value.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAV/CLEAR'.Clear (CLEAR)
:P.The clear for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*AFTER:EPK.
:PD.After the reference entry.
:PT.:PK.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.What is there is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAV/DTACPR'.Data compression (DTACPR)
:P.Whether the data is compressed as it is written.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DEV:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device.
:PT.:PK.*LOW:EPK.
:PD.Low.
:PT.:PK.*MEDIUM:EPK.
:PD.Medium.
:PT.:PK.*HIGH:EPK.
:PD.High.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ZLIB.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SAVCFG.Save Configuration (SAVCFG)
:P.Use the Save Configuration (SAVCFG) command to save the configuration
objects.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCFG/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SAVF:EPK.
:PD.A save file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MEDDFN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCFG/VOL'.Volume identifier (VOL)
:P.The volume identifier of the tape or optical volume. *MOUNTED uses
whatever volume is in the device.
:P.Up to 75 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*MOUNTED:EPK.
:PD.Whatever volume is in the device.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCFG/SEQNBR'.Sequence number (SEQNBR)
:P.The sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16777215.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCFG/LABEL'.File label (LABEL)
:P.The label of the file on the volume.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 17 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SAVCFG.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCFG/EXPDATE'.File expiration date (EXPDATE)
:P.The date after which the object or file can be deleted or
overwritten. *PERM means it never expires.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PERM:EPK.
:PD.Permanent&colon. it never expires.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCFG/ENDOPT'.End of media option (ENDOPT)
:P.What the device does with the tape when the operation ends&colon.
leave it where it is, rewind it, or rewind and unload it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REWIND:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound.
:PT.:PK.*LEAVE:EPK.
:PD.The tape stays where it is; the next operation goes on from there.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCFG/USEOPTBLK'.Use optimum block size (USEOPTBLK)
:P.Whether the device's optimum block size is used. The tape may then
not be readable on devices that do not support that size.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCFG/SAVF'.Save file (SAVF)
:P.The save file, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCFG/MEDDFN'.Media definition (MEDDFN)
:P.The media definition, which lists the devices and settings a parallel
save or restore uses.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCFG/OPTFILE'.Optical file (OPTFILE)
:P.The path of the file on the optical volume.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, '*' is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCFG/CLEAR'.Clear (CLEAR)
:P.The clear for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*AFTER:EPK.
:PD.After the reference entry.
:PT.:PK.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.What is there is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCFG/DTACPR'.Data compression (DTACPR)
:P.Whether the data is compressed as it is written.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DEV:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*LOW:EPK.
:PD.Low.
:PT.:PK.*MEDIUM:EPK.
:PD.Medium.
:PT.:PK.*HIGH:EPK.
:PD.High.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCFG/COMPACT'.Data compaction (COMPACT)
:P.Whether the device compacts data as it writes it to the tape.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DEV:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCFG/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PK.*OUTFILE:EPK.
:PD.The output goes to the database file named by OUTFILE.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCFG/OUTFILE'.File to receive output (OUTFILE)
:P.The database file that receives the output when OUTPUT(*OUTFILE) is
given. The file is created with the system's model format when it does
not exist.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCFG/OUTMBR'.Output member options (OUTMBR)
:P.The member of the output file that receives the records, and whether
they replace the member's records or are added after them.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Member to receive output
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first member of the file. A member with the file's name is added
when the file has none.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Replace or add records
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.The member's records are cleared first.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The records are added after the member's records.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SAVCHGOBJ.Save Changed Objects (SAVCHGOBJ)
:P.Use the Save Changed Objects (SAVCHGOBJ) command to save the objects
changed since a reference date.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/OBJ'.Objects (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/LIB'.Library (LIB)
:P.The library for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SAVF:EPK.
:PD.A save file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MEDDFN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/OBJTYPE'.Object types (OBJTYPE)
:P.The type or types of the objects the command works on.
:P.Up to 72 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 7 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/OBJJRN'.Journaled objects (OBJJRN)
:P.Whether to journaled objects.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/REFDATE'.Reference date (REFDATE)
:P.The reference date for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAVLIB:EPK.
:PD.The library the object was saved from.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/REFTIME'.Reference time (REFTIME)
:P.The reference time for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.time:EPV.
:PD.Type a time of day&colon. hours, minutes and seconds.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/VOL'.Volume identifier (VOL)
:P.The volume identifier of the tape or optical volume. *MOUNTED uses
whatever volume is in the device.
:P.Up to 75 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*MOUNTED:EPK.
:PD.Whatever volume is in the device.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/SEQNBR'.Sequence number (SEQNBR)
:P.The sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16777215.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/LABEL'.Label (LABEL)
:P.The label of the file on the volume.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 17 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LIB.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/EXPDATE'.File expiration date (EXPDATE)
:P.The date after which the object or file can be deleted or
overwritten. *PERM means it never expires.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PERM:EPK.
:PD.Permanent&colon. it never expires.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/ENDOPT'.End of media option (ENDOPT)
:P.What the device does with the tape when the operation ends&colon.
leave it where it is, rewind it, or rewind and unload it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REWIND:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound.
:PT.:PK.*LEAVE:EPK.
:PD.The tape stays where it is; the next operation goes on from there.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/SAVF'.Save file (SAVF)
:P.The save file, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/MEDDFN'.Media definition (MEDDFN)
:P.The media definition, which lists the devices and settings a parallel
save or restore uses.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/OPTFILE'.Optical file (OPTFILE)
:P.The path of the file on the optical volume.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, '*' is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/USEOPTBLK'.Use optimum block size (USEOPTBLK)
:P.Whether the device's optimum block size is used. The tape may then
not be readable on devices that do not support that size.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/TGTRLS'.Target release (TGTRLS)
:P.The release of the operating system the object is created for.
*CURRENT is this release; *PRV is the previous one.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.This release.
:PT.:PK.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/UPDHST'.Update history (UPDHST)
:P.Whether the save history of the objects is updated.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/CLEAR'.Clear (CLEAR)
:P.The clear for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*AFTER:EPK.
:PD.After the reference entry.
:PT.:PK.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.What is there is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/PRECHK'.Object pre-check (PRECHK)
:P.Whether every object is checked before any is saved or restored, and
the operation stopped if any cannot be.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/SAVACT'.Save active (SAVACT)
:P.Whether objects in use can be saved, and at which point of
consistency.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LIB, *SYNCLIB, *SYSDFN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/SAVACTWAIT'.Save active wait time (SAVACTWAIT)
:P.The save active wait time for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Object locks
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99999.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 120 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Pending record changes
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LOCKWAIT:EPK.
:PD.Waiting for a lock.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99999.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOCMTBDY.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Other pending changes
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LOCKWAIT:EPK.
:PD.Waiting for a lock.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/SAVACTMSGQ'.Save active message queue (SAVACTMSGQ)
:P.The save active message queue for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*WRKSTN:EPK.
:PD.The value of the workstation the job runs at.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/FILEMBR'.File member (FILEMBR)
:P.The file member for this command.
:P.Up to 50 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. File
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Member
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/ACCPTH'.Save access paths (ACCPTH)
:P.The save access paths for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/SAVFDTA'.Save file data (SAVFDTA)
:P.Whether to save file data.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/SPLFDTA'.Spooled file data (SPLFDTA)
:P.Whether the data of spooled files is saved with the output queues.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/QDTA'.Queue data (QDTA)
:P.The queue data for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DTAQ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/PVTAUT'.Private authorities (PVTAUT)
:P.Whether to private authorities.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/DTACPR'.Data compression (DTACPR)
:P.Whether the data is compressed as it is written.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DEV:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*LOW:EPK.
:PD.Low.
:PT.:PK.*MEDIUM:EPK.
:PD.Medium.
:PT.:PK.*HIGH:EPK.
:PD.High.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/COMPACT'.Data compaction (COMPACT)
:P.Whether the device compacts data as it writes it to the tape.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DEV:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/OMITLIB'.Libraries to omit (OMITLIB)
:P.Libraries that are not to be included.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/OMITOBJ'.Objects to omit (OMITOBJ)
:P.Objects that are not to be included.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Object
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Object type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ALRTBL:EPK.
:PD.Alert tables.
:PT.:PK.*BNDDIR:EPK.
:PD.Binding directories.
:PT.:PK.*CHTFMT:EPK.
:PD.Chart formats.
:PT.:PK.*CLD:EPK.
:PD.C locale descriptions.
:PT.:PK.*CLS:EPK.
:PD.Classes.
:PT.:PK.*CMD:EPK.
:PD.Commands.
:PT.:PK.*CRQD:EPK.
:PD.Change request descriptions.
:PT.:PK.*CSI:EPK.
:PD.Communications side information.
:PT.:PK.*CSPMAP:EPK.
:PD.Cross-system product maps.
:PT.:PK.*CSPTBL:EPK.
:PD.Cross-system product tables.
:PT.:PK.*DTAARA:EPK.
:PD.Data areas.
:PT.:PK.*DTADCT:EPK.
:PD.Data dictionaries.
:PT.:PK.*DTAQ:EPK.
:PD.Data queues.
:PT.:PK.*FCT:EPK.
:PD.Forms control tables.
:PT.:PK.*FILE:EPK.
:PD.Files&colon. physical, logical, display, printer, save, tape and DDM
files.
:PT.:PK.*FNTRSC:EPK.
:PD.Font resources.
:PT.:PK.*FNTTBL:EPK.
:PD.Font mapping tables.
:PT.:PK.*FORMDF:EPK.
:PD.Form definitions.
:PT.:PK.*FTR:EPK.
:PD.Filters.
:PT.:PK.*GSS:EPK.
:PD.Graphics symbol sets.
:PT.:PK.*IGCDCT:EPK.
:PD.Double-byte conversion dictionaries.
:PT.:PK.*IGCSRT:EPK.
:PD.Double-byte sort tables.
:PT.:PK.*IGCTBL:EPK.
:PD.Double-byte font tables.
:PT.:PK.*IMGCLG:EPK.
:PD.Image catalogs.
:PT.:PK.*JOBD:EPK.
:PD.Job descriptions.
:PT.:PK.*JOBQ:EPK.
:PD.Job queues.
:PT.:PK.*JRN:EPK.
:PD.Journals.
:PT.:PK.*JRNRCV:EPK.
:PD.Journal receivers.
:PT.:PK.*LOCALE:EPK.
:PD.Locales.
:PT.:PK.*MEDDFN:EPK.
:PD.Media definitions.
:PT.:PK.*MENU:EPK.
:PD.Menus.
:PT.:PK.*MGTCOL:EPK.
:PD.Management collections.
:PT.:PK.*MODULE:EPK.
:PD.Modules.
:PT.:PK.*MSGF:EPK.
:PD.Message files.
:PT.:PK.*MSGQ:EPK.
:PD.Message queues.
:PT.:PK.*M36:EPK.
:PD.System/36 machine descriptions.
:PT.:PK.*M36CFG:EPK.
:PD.System/36 machine configurations.
:PT.:PK.*NODGRP:EPK.
:PD.Node groups.
:PT.:PK.*NODL:EPK.
:PD.Node lists.
:PT.:PK.*NWSCFG:EPK.
:PD.Network server configurations.
:PT.:PK.*OUTQ:EPK.
:PD.Output queues.
:PT.:PK.*OVL:EPK.
:PD.Overlays.
:PT.:PK.*PAGDFN:EPK.
:PD.Page definitions.
:PT.:PK.*PAGSEG:EPK.
:PD.Page segments.
:PT.:PK.*PDFMAP:EPK.
:PD.PDF maps.
:PT.:PK.*PDG:EPK.
:PD.Print descriptor groups.
:PT.:PK.*PGM:EPK.
:PD.Programs.
:PT.:PK.*PNLGRP:EPK.
:PD.Panel groups.
:PT.:PK.*PSFCFG:EPK.
:PD.Print services configurations.
:PT.:PK.*QMFORM:EPK.
:PD.Query management forms.
:PT.:PK.*QMQRY:EPK.
:PD.Query management queries.
:PT.:PK.*QRYDFN:EPK.
:PD.Query definitions.
:PT.:PK.*SBSD:EPK.
:PD.Subsystem descriptions.
:PT.:PK.*SCHIDX:EPK.
:PD.Search indexes.
:PT.:PK.*SPADCT:EPK.
:PD.Spelling aid dictionaries.
:PT.:PK.*SQLPKG:EPK.
:PD.SQL packages.
:PT.:PK.*SQLUDT:EPK.
:PD.SQL user-defined types.
:PT.:PK.*SQLXSR:EPK.
:PD.SQL XML schema repositories.
:PT.:PK.*SRVPGM:EPK.
:PD.Service programs.
:PT.:PK.*SSND:EPK.
:PD.Session descriptions.
:PT.:PK.*S36:EPK.
:PD.The System/36 environment configuration.
:PT.:PK.*SVRSTG:EPK.
:PD.Server storage spaces.
:PT.:PK.*TBL:EPK.
:PD.Tables.
:PT.:PK.*TIMZON:EPK.
:PD.Time zone descriptions.
:PT.:PK.*USRIDX:EPK.
:PD.User indexes.
:PT.:PK.*USRQ:EPK.
:PD.User queues.
:PT.:PK.*USRSPC:EPK.
:PD.User spaces.
:PT.:PK.*VLDL:EPK.
:PD.Validation lists.
:PT.:PK.*WSCST:EPK.
:PD.Workstation customizing objects.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/ASPDEV'.ASP device (ASPDEV)
:P.The auxiliary storage pool device the command works in&colon. the
system ASP and basic user ASPs, or an independent ASP group.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SYSBAS:EPK.
:PD.The system ASP and the basic user ASPs.
:PT.:PK.*CURASPGRP:EPK.
:PD.The ASP group of the job's current thread.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PK.*OUTFILE:EPK.
:PD.The output goes to the database file named by OUTFILE.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/OUTFILE'.File to receive output (OUTFILE)
:P.The database file that receives the output when OUTPUT(*OUTFILE) is
given. The file is created with the system's model format when it does
not exist.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/OUTMBR'.Output member options (OUTMBR)
:P.The member of the output file that receives the records, and whether
they replace the member's records or are added after them.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Member to receive output
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first member of the file. A member with the file's name is added
when the file has none.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Replace or add records
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.The member's records are cleared first.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The records are added after the member's records.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVCHGOBJ/INFTYPE'.Type of output information (INFTYPE)
:P.The type of output information for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*MBR:EPK.
:PD.The member.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ, *LIB, *ERR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=SAVLIB.Save Library (SAVLIB)
:P.Use the Save Library (SAVLIB) command to save libraries to a device
or a save file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/LIB'.Library (LIB)
:P.The library for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NONSYS, *IBM.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Up to 4 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SAVF:EPK.
:PD.A save file.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MEDDFN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/VOL'.Volume identifier (VOL)
:P.The volume identifier of the tape or optical volume. *MOUNTED uses
whatever volume is in the device.
:P.Up to 75 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*MOUNTED:EPK.
:PD.Whatever volume is in the device.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/SEQNBR'.Sequence number (SEQNBR)
:P.The sequence number for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*END:EPK.
:PD.The end.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16777215.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/LABEL'.File label (LABEL)
:P.The label of the file on the volume.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 17 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LIB.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/EXPDATE'.File expiration date (EXPDATE)
:P.The date after which the object or file can be deleted or
overwritten. *PERM means it never expires.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PERM:EPK.
:PD.Permanent&colon. it never expires.
:PT.:PV.date:EPV.
:PD.Type a date in the date format of the job.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/ENDOPT'.End of media option (ENDOPT)
:P.What the device does with the tape when the operation ends&colon.
leave it where it is, rewind it, or rewind and unload it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REWIND:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound.
:PT.:PK.*LEAVE:EPK.
:PD.The tape stays where it is; the next operation goes on from there.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/STRLIB'.Starting library (STRLIB)
:P.The starting library for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first one.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/SAVF'.Save file (SAVF)
:P.The save file, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/MEDDFN'.Media definition (MEDDFN)
:P.The media definition, which lists the devices and settings a parallel
save or restore uses.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/OPTFILE'.Optical file (OPTFILE)
:P.The path of the file on the optical volume.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 256 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, '*' is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/USEOPTBLK'.Use optimum block size (USEOPTBLK)
:P.Whether the device's optimum block size is used. The tape may then
not be readable on devices that do not support that size.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/TGTRLS'.Target release (TGTRLS)
:P.The release of the operating system the object is created for.
*CURRENT is this release; *PRV is the previous one.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURRENT:EPK.
:PD.This release.
:PT.:PK.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/UPDHST'.Update history (UPDHST)
:P.Whether the save history of the objects is updated.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/CLEAR'.Clear (CLEAR)
:P.The clear for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*AFTER:EPK.
:PD.After the reference entry.
:PT.:PK.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.What is there is replaced.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/PRECHK'.Object pre-check (PRECHK)
:P.Whether every object is checked before any is saved or restored, and
the operation stopped if any cannot be.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/SAVACT'.Save active (SAVACT)
:P.Whether objects in use can be saved, and at which point of
consistency.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LIB, *SYNCLIB, *SYSDFN.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/SAVACTWAIT'.Save active wait time (SAVACTWAIT)
:P.The save active wait time for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 3 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Object locks
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99999.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, 120 is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Pending record changes
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LOCKWAIT:EPK.
:PD.Waiting for a lock.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99999.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *NOCMTBDY.
:H4.Part 3&colon. Other pending changes
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LOCKWAIT:EPK.
:PD.Waiting for a lock.
:PT.:PK.*NOMAX:EPK.
:PD.No limit.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 0 to 99999.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/SAVACTMSGQ'.Save active message queue (SAVACTMSGQ)
:P.The save active message queue for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*WRKSTN:EPK.
:PD.The value of the workstation the job runs at.
:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/ACCPTH'.Save access paths (ACCPTH)
:P.The save access paths for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SYSVAL:EPK.
:PD.The value of the system value that holds the default.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/SAVFDTA'.Save file data (SAVFDTA)
:P.Whether to save file data.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/SPLFDTA'.Spooled file data (SPLFDTA)
:P.Whether the data of spooled files is saved with the output queues.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/QDTA'.Queue data (QDTA)
:P.The queue data for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *DTAQ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/DTACPR'.Data compression (DTACPR)
:P.Whether the data is compressed as it is written.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DEV:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*LOW:EPK.
:PD.Low.
:PT.:PK.*MEDIUM:EPK.
:PD.Medium.
:PT.:PK.*HIGH:EPK.
:PD.High.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/COMPACT'.Data compaction (COMPACT)
:P.Whether the device compacts data as it writes it to the tape.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DEV:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/OMITLIB'.Libraries to omit (OMITLIB)
:P.Libraries that are not to be included.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SAVLIB/OMITOBJ'.Objects to omit (OMITOBJ)
:P.Objects that are not to be included.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Object
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Object type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
